👑🧠 Birbal and the Farmer’s Well (Raw Story)

One day, a farmer came to Emperor Akbar.

He said, “Your Majesty, I sold my well to a man. But now he says the water inside still belongs to him!”

Akbar was confused and asked Birbal to solve the case.

Birbal called the buyer and asked, “Did you buy the well?”

“Yes,” the man said.

Birbal then asked, “Then why are you keeping your water in someone else’s well?”

The man was shocked.

Birbal continued, “If the well belongs to the farmer, you cannot keep your water in it. Either take your water away or pay rent.”

The man realized his mistake and agreed.

Akbar praised Birbal for his clever judgment.

💖 Moral:

Justice requires clear and logical thinking.
